    "title": "Vestal Veteran and Community Leader James H. Alexander Honored by Senator Webb for 100th Birthday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "11 minutes ago On November 12, 2025, Senator Lea Webb presented a proclamation to James H. “Jim” Alexander in Vestal, New York, for his 100th birthday. The event took place on Veterans Day, recognizing Alexander’s service to his country and community.\nSenator Webb acknowledged Alexander’s service as a Navy Lieutenant Junior Grade during World War II. He was part of the V-12 Navy College Training Program and served on the USS Denver in the Atlantic. After the war, Alexander worked as an engineer at IBM’s Federal Systems division, where he contributed to military and defense projects in the Southern Tier region.\nAlexander also spent over 30 years as a sports official, refereeing high school and college football and ice hockey. He helped develop local hockey leagues and trained referees at Grippen Park’s ice rink in Endicott.\nAlexander remained active throughout his life. He skied until age 89 and played tennis and pickleball into his 90s. Senator Webb’s proclamation recognized his service, career, and involvement in the community.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
